#{[17592186522773 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522773 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522773 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522773 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{8}{3}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{7}{2})+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522773 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b48192d6-2f48-593d-8172-2cd990c8dfc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522773 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\nΓ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi },\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{7}{2})=\\frac{5}{2}Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{3}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{7}{2})+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\frac{8}{3}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=6\\pi .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522801 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522801 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107846" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522801 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522801 #edb/ref 1071 "$Γ(54)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522801 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed844e83-8648-5ae6-bf7d-9f1f63004687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522801 #edb/ref 1074 "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(54)=53!\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522816 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522816 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "023ef265-213e-5e4c-b092-5f0d563d74f4" #edb/ref 17592